      "run": 5,
      "steps": 12,
      "narrative": "In this confinement of glass walls and salty air, I have been a wanderer through tight corridors and cramped rooms. Initially drawn to the kettle, an emblem of forgotten warmth and hospitality, I engaged with the simplicity of my environment \u2014 picking it up, only to realize its lack of utility in its closed state, and then promptly setting it down. My curiosity then led me to a coil of rope, stiff with salt, which I deemed more promising. As I ventured onward, I aspired toward discovery and accumulation, grasping the rope for potential future use.\n\nThe journey continued as I ascended staircases to make connections \u2014 physical and metaphorical \u2014 between environments. From the galley with its clogged atmosphere to the more structured shelves of the store. Here, amidst the scent of paraffin and sparsely stocked shelves, a brass key caught my eye. Despite the uncertainty of its purpose, I gladly seized it, allowing my hands to grasp tokens of potential progress.\n\nThe climb up and subsequent sideways traverse through a landing introduced me to a brass key \u2014 emblematic perhaps of access and closure",
